---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const updated = '2026-11-03';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Aftertone"
  description="Aftertone collects nothing: no account system, no analytics. Your music, credentials and listening history stay on your device and your own media server."
  lang="en"
  path="/en/privacy"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">
      Effective: {updated}　Last updated: {updated}　<a href={withBase('/privacy')}>简体中文版</a>
    </p>

    <div class="legal">
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:24px">
        <p style="margin:0">
          Aftertone has no account system and no cloud service. Your music files, server credentials, listening history and settings stay on your own device and your own media server. We do not collect, upload or sell your data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="legal-callout" id="no-tracking">
        <h2>Data Not Used to Track You</h2>
        <p>
          Aftertone does not use your data to track you across apps or websites owned by other companies.
          We do not link your activity in Aftertone to your identity, to advertising identifiers, or to data collected by third parties.
          The app contains no advertising or analytics SDKs, and on iOS we do not request App Tracking Transparency authorization.
          In App Store terms, none of the data described in this policy is used to track you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to the Aftertone clients we distribute for Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iOS.
        Aftertone is a local music player that connects to a media server you run or choose yourself. We do not provide music content or cloud storage.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account registration; we never ask for your name, phone number, email or identity documents.</li>
        <li>No device or advertising identifiers, precise location, contacts, photos or other information unrelated to playback.</li>
        <li>No analytics, crash reporting, advertising or social SDKs are bundled.</li>
        <li>No cross-app or cross-site tracking; on iOS we do not request App Tracking Transparency authorization.</li>
        <li>We do not sell, rent or share your data, and we do not use it for ad profiling or model training.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Data processed only on your device</h2>
      <p>The following data is created and stored locally and never passes through us:</p>
      <div class="legal-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Storage</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Media server address, username, password or token</td>
              <td>Connecting to and signing in to your server</td>
              <td>System secure storage (iOS/macOS Keychain, Android Keystore, Windows DPAPI, Linux libsecret)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Library metadata, cover and image cache</td>
              <td>Browsing, search and playback</td>
              <td>App-private directories and local database</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Play history, favorites, playlists, search history</td>
              <td>Recent plays, statistics and ordering</td>
              <td>Local database</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Downloaded audio and cached lyrics</td>
              <td>Offline playback</td>
              <td>App-private directories</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Settings, theme, equalizer parameters</td>
              <td>Remembering your preferences</td>
              <td>Local storage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Backup files you export</td>
              <td>Migration and restore</td>
              <td>A location you choose</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>4. When the app uses the network</h2>
      <p>
        Network requests happen only in the cases below. They are sent directly from your device to the corresponding service; we do not relay them or receive their contents.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Scenario</th><th>What is sent</th><th>Recipient</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Connecting and playback</td>
              <td>Server address, credentials, playback and sync requests</td>
              <td>The media server you run or choose (Navidrome, Subsonic, Jellyfin, Emby, Plex, etc.)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Cross-device sync</td>
              <td>Playback progress, favorites and similar state</td>
              <td>The same media server you configured</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Lyrics lookup</td>
              <td>Track title, artist, album and duration</td>
              <td>LRCLIB (lrclib.net), a public lyrics API</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Update check</td>
              <td>IP address, User-Agent and standard request headers</td>
              <td>GitHub Releases API (api.github.com)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Downloading a new version</td>
              <td>As above</td>
              <td>App distribution platform or a third-party mirror you choose</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        These third-party services are operated independently and are governed by their own privacy policies. You can reduce these requests by not using the lyrics fallback or by disabling automatic update checks.
      </p>

      <h2>5. System permissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>iOS</strong>: Local Network access is used to discover and connect to media servers on your LAN; Background Audio keeps playback running when the screen is locked or you switch apps. If you deny Local Network access, you can still connect via a public address, but automatic LAN discovery will not work.</li>
        <li><strong>Android</strong>: We request network access, wake lock and a media playback foreground service for background playback and downloads. We do not request storage, location, contacts or camera permissions.</li>
        <li><strong>macOS / Windows / Linux</strong>: Network access to your server, plus read/write access to app-private caches and downloads; exporting a backup only accesses the folder you select.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Local data remains on your device until you delete it. You can clear caches and statistics in the app, clear app data in system settings, or uninstall the app; each of these removes the corresponding data.
        Export a backup first if you want to keep your data.
        Play history and favorites stored on your media server are controlled by the server administrator, and deletion depends on the server software you use.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Aftertone is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. Minors should use the app under the guidance of a guardian.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated as the app evolves; the "Last updated" date at the top of this page will change accordingly. For material changes to data handling, we will notify you on this website or in the app.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this policy or how data is handled, please reach us via
        <a href="https://github.com/DeeGor168/aftertone/issues" rel="noopener">GitHub Issues</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-meta" style="margin-top:32px">
        <a href={withBase('/en/')}>Back to home</a>　<a href={withBase('/privacy')}>简体中文版</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
